# Q: does the ship actually arrive, and does it arrive the same way twice?
#
# The phase 0 gate in probe form. A hundred-tonne crewed hull launches two kilometres down
# a station's corridor with the station's own orbital velocity, and the world runs at 120 Hz
# until it is either captured or past.
#
#   dotnet run --project src/SolSystem.Probe -- \
#       --probe tools/probe/docking.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/docking.txt
#
# The hash at the end is the reason this exists. Two runs have to produce the same one, and
# if they do not then something in the simulation is reading a clock, an iteration order or
# a float -- which it would also do in a played game, where it is far harder to notice.

launch Meridian 2000 0.0
phase
range

# Half a minute.
advance 3600
range
closing
ship

# The approach, until it is either in the envelope or clearly not going to be.
advance 12000
phase
range
closing

expect "the ship closed inside the capture range" range 2.0 less
expect "the ship is slow enough for the latches" closing 0.5 less
expect "the ship is in the terminal phase" phase 2 exactly

hash docking
